  "notes": [
   "Keyed by the subtype ids used in units_dictionary.json and SupplementalLexicon.cs.",
   "factorNum/factorDen (and offsetNum/offsetDen for affine temperature units) are exact integer rationals; canonical = value * factor + offset. Consumers compare via cross-multiplication, never division, so non-terminating rationals (month = year/12) stay exact.",
   "Two quantities convert only when their dimension strings are equal. Consumption's reciprocal pair (mile-per-gallon vs liter-per-100-kilometer) lands on reciprocal dimensions and is deliberately not cross-converted.",
   "Only USD carries a subunit pair (USD-cent); all other currencies have no entries, so cross-currency pairs never convert.",
   "concentr-permillion and concentr-portion-per-1e9 are legacy ids from the babel-era dictionary, resolved as part-per-1000000 and part-per-1000000000.",
   "semantically_distinct entries carry a distinct: dimension of their own: CLDR's dimensional algebra or aliasing would equate them with a different physical claim, so they keep same-subtype matching but never cross-convert."
  ],
